// EXPECT: error
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: a closure may not return a reference
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: this body's value has type `&Int`, which is a reference
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: references in Saw are PARAMETERS ONLY
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: yield the value instead (drop the `&`, so the closure returns `Int`)
//
// DF-163d: design 163a refuses a written `-> &T` at the declaration, and a
// closure literal writes no return type at all -- so `{ &x }` typed `() -> &Int`
// and handed a pointer to `x` out past the call that made it. Inference is the
// only place the rule can be applied, so the error is reported there, anchored
// at the body's tail expression. The `with_ref` identity closure `{ e in e }` is
// NOT this case: reading a reference binding yields the value.

func main() {
    let x = 7
    let f = { &x }
    let v = f()
    print("{v}")
}
